WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:04.422 --> 00:00:06.263
SCARLETT JOHANSSON
From the very beginning, when we first

00:00:06.313 --> 00:00:09.325
started talking about doing this
Black Widow standalone film,

00:00:09.375 --> 00:00:17.140
there was no reason to do it
unless we could really dig deep.

00:00:18.493 --> 00:00:20.138
KEVIN FEIGE
Black Widow had an enormous amount

00:00:20.188 --> 00:00:23.216
of her past that has
never been explored before.

00:00:23.266 --> 00:00:26.349
And what's fun about doing that now
is that we get to see Scarlett

00:00:26.399 --> 00:00:30.365
as this amazing, amazing actor
and performer, with an entirely new

00:00:30.415 --> 00:00:32.230
cast of characters in this film.

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.338
SCARLETT JOHANSSON
I've, of course, over the years, thought

00:00:34.389 --> 00:00:37.667
about what it could be, but it never
would have been able to be as

00:00:37.717 --> 00:00:41.581
fully realized as it is now,
because I've spent over

00:00:41.631 --> 00:00:43.416
a decade of time with this character.

00:00:47.116 --> 00:00:48.497
SCARLETT JOHANSSON
I would love to take this character in

00:00:48.547 --> 00:00:52.942
every different direction. I think she
certainly encounters her fair share

00:00:52.992 --> 00:00:54.325
of the Marvel universe.

00:00:54.375 --> 00:00:55.630
JON FAVREAU
The part that appealed to me most

00:00:55.680 --> 00:00:58.520
about her is her
dedication and just her intelligence.

00:00:58.570 --> 00:01:02.161
She really helped design the costume,
helped to flesh out the character.

00:01:02.211 --> 00:01:03.778
SCARLETT JOHANSSON
To be a part of this is pretty exciting.

00:01:03.828 --> 00:01:06.261
I didn't know how
the fans would respond.

00:01:07.381 --> 00:01:11.534
I think that there's so much to explore
with Black Widow. Her past is something

00:01:11.584 --> 00:01:13.284
that's always been shrouded in mystery.

00:01:13.334 --> 00:01:14.354
STEVE ROGERS
You know it's kind of hard to trust

00:01:14.404 --> 00:01:16.783
trust someone when you
don't know who that someone really is.

00:01:17.605 --> 00:01:18.258
NATASHA ROMANOFF
Yeah.

00:01:18.308 --> 00:01:21.807
SCARLETT JOHANSSON
Really the most important aspect of my job

00:01:21.857 --> 00:01:25.666
is to keep a
sort of steady evolution.

00:01:26.349 --> 00:01:28.947
She has a greater calling.

00:01:28.998 --> 00:01:30.182
NATASHA ROMANOFF
The last five years, I've been trying to

00:01:30.232 --> 00:01:32.206
do one thing:
Get to right here.

00:01:32.256 --> 00:01:34.484
That's all it's been about,
bringing everybody back.

00:01:34.534 --> 00:01:37.101
SCARLETT JOHANSSON
This character who has searched her

00:01:37.151 --> 00:01:41.108
whole life for a purpose,
actually finds her purpose.

00:01:41.159 --> 00:01:42.475
NATASHA ROMANOFF
It's okay.

00:01:46.664 --> 00:01:50.294
JOE RUSSO
It's the single most heroic moment

00:01:50.344 --> 00:01:52.026
in the history of the Marvel universe.

00:01:54.320 --> 00:01:55.678
KEVIN FEIGE
You know, the hope was always to be able

00:01:55.728 --> 00:01:58.544
to do much more with Black Widow.
And with each appearance and with

00:01:58.594 --> 00:02:01.068
each interaction
growing and evolving her,

00:02:01.118 --> 00:02:03.871
all, frankly, building to
her standalone movie now.

00:02:06.063 --> 00:02:08.552
SCARLETT JOHANSSON
We had the opportunity in this for

00:02:08.602 --> 00:02:12.335
some sort of healing.
And I think you really feel that.

00:02:12.412 --> 00:02:14.239
KEVIN FEIGE
The way Scarlett portrays this hero

00:02:14.289 --> 00:02:17.474
in this movie is bigger and better
than anything you've seen her do

00:02:17.524 --> 00:02:19.292
in any of the Marvel movies.

00:02:19.342 --> 00:02:21.055
SCARLETT JOHANSSON
It's gonna let people see

00:02:22.399 --> 00:02:24.142
who Natasha really is.

00:02:31.207 --> 00:02:32.859
NATASHA ROMANOFF
I've lived a lot of lives.

